WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.770
An airport lounge.

2
00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:03.440
A school library.

3
00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:05.270
A quiet hillside.

4
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.800
A Muslim unrolls a small mat.

5
00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:12.310
First comes water:
hands, mouth, face, arms,

6
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.990
and feet to the ankles.

7
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:17.890
Then one direction, the same
for every Muslim on Earth:

8
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.060
towards the Ka'bah in Makkah.

9
00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:22.650
Five times a day, wherever they are.

10
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.840
So what happens in those
few minutes, and why?

11
00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:28.940
In this mission, you'll
follow one rak'ah of prayer,

12
00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:31.010
from standing to prostration.

13
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:34.030
Then you'll read the words
that open every prayer,

14
00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.720
and find out what prayer means to Muslims.

15
00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:40.640
Your mission: find out what happens
in those few minutes of prayer,

16
00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:42.270
and why Muslims keep them.
